{{!
    @template tool_vae/booklet_authorize_page

    The page of the managers authorized to produce the archive of the structure, below its heading: what an authorization
    is, then one sentence when nobody may be authorized, or the table of the managers.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\booklet_authorize_page. The template holds no
    logic. Every text is escaped (double braces), except one key of HTML made by another template (triple braces):
    tablehtml, a table drawn by the template tool_vae/table (the names and states in it are escaped by the template
    tool_vae/cell_content, the buttons drawn by the template tool_vae/booklet_authorize_form).

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * intro - string, what an authorization is
    * none - false, or a string: the sentence drawn when nobody may be authorized
    * tablehtml - false, or HTML: the table of the managers

    Example context (json):
    {
        "intro": "A manager you authorize here may produce the archive of the structure of every vaeiste they follow.",
        "none": false,
        "tablehtml": "<table class=\"generaltable tool-vae-bookletauth\"><tbody><tr><td>Marie Lefèvre</td></tr></tbody></table>"
    }
}}
<p>{{intro}}</p>
{{#none}}
<p>{{none}}</p>
{{/none}}
{{#tablehtml}}
{{{tablehtml}}}
{{/tablehtml}}
